sequenceDiagram
	autonumber
	actor Customer
	participant Storefront
	participant Ordering as Ordering API
	participant Basket as Basket API
	participant Catalog as Catalog API
	participant Finance
	participant Kafka
	participant Notification
	participant SMTP as SMTP Provider

	Customer ->> Storefront: Confirm checkout
	Storefront ->> Ordering: Create Order
	Ordering ->> Basket: Read persisted basket
	Basket -->> Ordering: Item quantities
	Ordering ->> Catalog: Resolve current book prices
	Catalog -->> Ordering: Book details and prices
	Ordering ->> Ordering: Persist New Order and price snapshot

	par Immediate checkout confirmation
		Ordering -->> Storefront: Order accepted
		Storefront -->> Customer: Display confirmation
	and Asynchronous post-checkout coordination
		Ordering -->> Finance: UserCheckedOutIntegrationEvent
		Finance ->> Finance: Start tracked orchestration
		Finance ->> Kafka: Publish PlaceOrderCommand
		Finance ->> Finance: Schedule 30-minute timeout

		par Basket cleanup consumer
			Kafka ->> Basket: PlaceOrderCommand
			Basket ->> Basket: Delete submitted basket

			alt Deletion succeeds
				Basket -->> Finance: BasketDeletedCompleteIntegrationEvent
				Finance ->> Kafka: DeleteBasketCompleteCommand
				Kafka ->> Ordering: Log cleanup completion
			else Deletion fails
				Basket -->> Finance: BasketDeletedFailedIntegrationEvent
				Finance ->> Finance: Mark failure and finalize orchestration
				Finance ->> Kafka: DeleteBasketFailedCommand
				Kafka ->> Ordering: Soft-delete Order if present
				Note over Ordering: Preserves New status; no cancellation event
			end
		and Notification consumer
			Kafka ->> Notification: PlaceOrderCommand
			Notification ->> Notification: Check Redis idempotency guard

			alt Recipient email is present
				Notification ->> SMTP: Submit order email over SMTP
				alt Submission succeeds
					SMTP -->> Notification: Accepted
				else Submission fails after retries
					Notification ->> Kafka: Route to dead-letter queue
				end
			else Recipient email is absent
				Notification ->> Notification: Skip email delivery
			end
			Note over Notification,SMTP: SMTP acceptance confirms handoff, not inbox delivery
		and Finance timeout policy
			loop Timeout fires while active (up to 2 reissues)
				Finance ->> Finance: Increment retry count
				Finance ->> Kafka: Reissue PlaceOrderCommand
				Finance ->> Finance: Schedule next 30-minute timeout
			end

			opt Retry budget exhausted
				Finance ->> Finance: Cancel and finalize orchestration
				opt Customer name and email present
					Finance ->> Kafka: CancelOrderCommand
					Kafka ->> Notification: Request cancellation email only
				end
				Note over Finance,Ordering: Orchestration cancellation does not cancel the Order
			end
		end
		Note over Basket,Notification: Consumers run independently; retries may repeat work
	end
